# =========================================================================
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Nothing here may carry a credential.
# =========================================================================
# The gateway's real settings live in config.py: the database password and
# every server's API key. Only config.example.py, which ships placeholders,
# belongs in the repo.
#
# Matched by pattern, not by path, so a new per-release kit -
# gateway-1.0.16/, gateway-1.0.18/, or whatever ships next - is covered the
# moment it is created. A path-literal rule covered only gateway/ and left
# the per-release folders open.
#
# The gateway itself writes timestamped config.py.bak-<stamp> copies when it
# maintains the file, and Windows leaves "config - Copy.py" behind. Both hold
# the same secrets as the original, so both are matched.
gateway*/config*
!gateway*/config.example.py
config.py
config*.bak-*
config - Copy.py

# Server-side secrets an admin may leave next to the kit while setting up.
# HFWastelandZ_secrets.conf holds the API key that pairs with config.py.
*secrets.conf
!*secrets.conf.example

# Database dumps. The backup step in the upgrade guide writes these into
# whatever directory the admin happens to be standing in, which is often the
# kit. A dump is the entire player database in plain text.
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*-backup-*.sql
wastelandz*.sql

# Local Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Local databases and OS clutter
*.db
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
